    "turn_text": "All right, a few things in your montage that I want to address. On the Ukraine front, we have some breaking news there. Literally, just as we were getting set to go on the air, Zelensky has put out now a Zelensky has put out a follow-up statement. What happened at the White House was regrettable. We need to negotiate for peace. I'd like to sign your minerals deal, basically a complete and total capitulation in terms of the press release. But we've been here before. because he was really just supposed to come and thank America and sign the deal and, you know, get a check and let's negotiate and end this thing. And he chose not to do that. So now he is feigning some level of humility. You know, if Todd were here, faith without works is dead. So we'll see if he follows through. But at least rhetorically, there is some form of a capitulation there that we should mention just because it's a corollary to one of the main stories in your montage and it literally just came in here in the last few minutes. I like and I want to take the juxtaposition of Democrats all voting against protecting women from men in their sports, and from leering at them and assaulting them in their locker rooms and private oasis. And Elizabeth Warren, you had these clips kind of back to back. I want to expand that further. Elizabeth Warren bringing a fired federal worker with her to the state of the union. I just draw me the composite and I think this is, this is something that's very important. All of you within the sound of my voice. This is the way you need to talk to a lot of Republicans. You need to lay things out for them like this. Like for example, we had some squishes down the stretch here and getting rid of the gender madness in Iowa. We took, we took Trump's comments putting the main governor on blast and we club them over the head with it. down the stretch. And I do think that was vital in us getting the vote to secure at the down the stretch. And we need to warn and constantly scold even these Republicans, you're genuflecting to people who will never vote for you. Never. So what, what, why? Why are you doing this? If you just agree with them, just be honest with me and go join their party. We have a party for that belief system already. Go join them. But what is the point in pandering and genuflecting to people? I understand human nature. I'm a biblical worldview guy, so I think I understand it pretty well. I've read the user's manual a few times. So I understand genuflecting and pandering in order to get a result, okay? Like I understand a woman who has interest in a man letting him have the milk for free because she wants him to buy the cow. I understand a man taking a shower and actually applying deodorant and cleaning out his car before a first date because he likes the girl and wants to make a good first impression. I understand pandering and genuflecting to someone you or a group you might actually think you have a shot with. If you've never worked in politics, which you don't understand is because I know of no other walk of life where this is the case, by the way. I mean, Aaron, think of another industry or sector of the culture where there is pandering and genuflecting to people who will never come around to supporting you no matter how hard you do it than in politics. I don't know of",
