    "turn_text": "Well, a couple of things that we're doing that you alluded to the hearing that's being held this afternoon, and it's a subcommittee that's going to be looking at the just how these elected are proud of these local prosecutors and state prosecutors are utilizing this law fair. I mean, we saw it so much with President Trump, not only in his first term, the things, but when he came out of that term, just the way that the prosecutors at the state and the local just sort of went after him. And of course, as you mentioned, you've got these judges that are trying to step in and block his executive orders at every point in turn, all trying to throw up barriers, all trying to slow down the progress of what the American people voted for in November of 24. And I think that what we're trying to do this afternoon, at least in this initial hearing, is just look at the approach that they take and begin to expose those kind of things. But I think one of the things that's going to happen with these judges is there is certainly a move that is afoot to file impeachment against these federal judges. that are just stepping in that is way outside the bounds of what they are doing and just trying to stop and slow down. Again, just throw up barriers in every turn and that's using our legal system for a purpose that is not intended. And you know, it's kind of like if you can't win at the ballot box, you just sue until it's blue. I think was the theme that they oftentimes used.",
