    "turn_text": "Well, I do think that that time is as quickly coming as people are looking at all different avenues of approaches that we can have. You know, one of the things that we were grateful for, and I think it showed just the problem and the extent of it when you had the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court single-handedly stepping in last week and hitting the pause button on a decision of a judge that was saying that You know, they couldn't slow down or stop this funding of USAID. And I think that it was important that Judge Roberts, I think it sent a message that it took the Chief Justice himself to speak out because I think you're right. I think people do recognize the different branches of government. And I think that they recognize that the courts are that third branch, if you will. And it's very important that the Congress do understand our responsibility that when they get so out of white that we do have to step in and we do have to take action. And that's one of the things that, again, we're discussing even today in this hearing is a bill by Congressman Fry from South Carolina that's called But it's probably ending political prosecutions and executive retaliation act of 2025. Congressman Russell Fry is a sponsor of that bill. And those are the kind of things that we are looking toward.",
