    "turn_idx": 64,
    "turn_text": "Let's switch gears. The other paradigm shift is birthright citizenship and the president is attempting to go back to what the original meaning of the 14th amendment was. If you read the senator from Michigan, Jacob Hall, I believe was his name, is one of the main authors of the 14th amendment and what he thought that it meant. He was even questioned at the time. Hey, does this mean any foreigner comes in here and as a kid, they're a citizen and he's like, I, well, I'm just assuming we're all assuming it's the original implication that you had to be. That's why it says under the jurisdiction thereof. And he said, that's why we don't trust what we don't count the children of ambassadors as citizens and things of that nature. They're not here under the jurisdiction of the United States government. Right. And so this was really how this was interpreted until well into the 20th century when it was expanded to basically just bypass immigration law. Obviously you guys are working on this in that subcommittee as well. So where's this battle heading? Would you tell us",
