    "turn_idx": 66,
    "turn_text": "you know, I'm excited, obviously, about the president on January 20th issued his executive order that made it clear that he was going to protect the meaning and value of what it meant to be a citizen. American citizenship means something. It's a valued gift that we're very grateful for. And the President's executive order was the start. I'm very excited to be a co-sponsor on a bill by Brian Babin, Representative Babin from Texas, has introduced a bill that really is going to help clarify this whole issue and codify it. And I'm excited. I'm hoping this bill continues to move forward because it's going to do that. Ultimately, you're going to see, I guess, the courts, President, when he knew that executive, put that executive order in place, He knew that it was going to be challenged in court. It's going to make its way back up, I assume, to the Supreme Court. And my hope is that the court we have is going to find correctly. We do have a majority on the Supreme Court currently that are originalist and do believe in the original intent of what was written there. And we all know. Every American knows that the 14th Amendment was not put in place so that illegal aliens could come across the border and have babies that instantly become American citizens. That was not the intent of it at all. And so I'm confident as we work our way through the courts, but from our role in Congress, while it's important to have an executive order, That's only as strong as the next president that comes in and tries to rewrite it. And then the court's interpretation is critical. And I think we need to hear from them. But Congress can codify this. And I think it's important that we take that step. And that's why I'm a co-sponsor of Representative Babin's bill, that I think is really important in moving it forward.",
