    "turn_text": "My findings in Western Pennsylvania almost eight months later right now. On July 13, 2024, a seemingly mild-mannered college kid almost altered the course of human history when he shot Donald Trump at a rally in Butler, Pennsylvania. But to friends, neighbors, former teachers and investigators, why Thomas Crooks did what he did is just as much of a mystery now as it was back then. Videographer Matt McDermott and I spent a week in Butler, Pennsylvania and nearby Bethel Park in a sometimes wild journey to find out what really happened. After all these months, the trail is as cold as the ground that you see in front of me. The motive remains unknown. Why? What we found shocked us, even though Thomas Cook's killed one rally-goer, Cori Comparator, and seriously injured two others while grazing Trump's right ear, there's a lot of sympathy for him in his hometown of Bethel Park. Several people told us they don't think Crooks acted alone and that he might have been a patsy. Some also accused Biden's FBI of suppressing some information, like why Crooks' body was cremated so quickly and what his overseas encrypted accounts revealed. Private investigator Doug Hagman's had a team of seven working on this mystery after being hired by a secret client shortly after the event. He says his team used a technique called geofencing. Hagman told me they located eight or nine devices, probably cell phones, that belonged to other people, but were pinpointed to being with crooks at his home, at his old high school, at his gun club, and even at the rally. Hagman said he doesn't believe Crooks acted alone and that he was part of a criminal network that's still out there and still wants to kill President",
